<title>HONG KONG: Wah Kwong interim net down 29.7 percent.</title>
<headline>Wah Kwong interim net down 29.7 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million US$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (U.S. cents)	   16.0  vs 22.9</p>
<p>    Dividend (U.S. cents)    1.5   vs 1.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil   vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    20.41 vs 29.05</p>
<p>    Turnover		     78.18 vs 75.69 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		 Wah Kwong Shipping Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  December 16-20</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   December 30</p>
<p>NOTE - Wah Kwong Shipping Holdings is a ship-owning group.</p>
<p>Comparative turnover has been restated to include the sale proceeds received instead of the profit arising from disposal of owned vessels in order to be consistent with the revenue recognition policy adopted for the current period.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
